meta {
  name: POST honkandflash (flash only)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/vehicle/v1/vehicles/{{vin}}/honkandflash
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "mode": "flash",
    "duration_s": 10
  }
}

docs {
  v2.15.5 (#543 follow-up) — CARIAD-BFF flash for VW EU + Audi uses
  the honkandflash command endpoint. The older vehicleLights/flash
  endpoint was a guessed shape and returns 400.

  mode is the serial name the apps send ("flash", "honkandflash"), not
  the enum constant name (FLASH_ONLY, HONK_AND_FLASH).

  userPosition is a required element of the request in the apps. When a
  last-known position is available, VWEUClient.command_flash() sends it
  with the first request, as "userPosition": {"latitude": ...,
  "longitude": ...}, and the answer to that request is final. The body
  above is the form without a position; the integration sends it only
  when no position is known.

  Implementation: VWEUClient.command_flash() in cariad/api/vw_eu.py.
  Audi inherits.
}
